-- title:
--   Regularity of the Gauss-centred special fibre at q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ be an integer not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ equal to $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, i.e. the subfield of $L(\!(X)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH (q^2*M'))`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L76), where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L(\!(X)\!)$ the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_L(\mathrm{jq})$, where $\mathrm{jq}=X^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ satisfying: $f \in W_0$ if and only if there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ as Laurent series over $L$ (the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Write $\mathfrak{X} = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}(A,K,j)$, the pushout of the two charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$, the rings of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ and over $A[j^{-1}]$ respectively. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ via the structure morphism $\mathfrak{X} \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Assume further that $z$ is the image under the chart inclusion of a point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ whose prime ideal is not maximal, and that every element $b$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in the prime of $y$. Then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the $q=2$ instance of the assertion that the component of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X(\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))$ cut out by the Gauss valuation ring — the $\infty$-Igusa branch — is reduced, equivalently that the Gauss ring is unramified over $A$; the point $z$ in question is the generic point of that component. It feeds the construction of an open subscheme of the integral model that is smooth over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_of_forall_not_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_opens_smooth_comp_toBase_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_of_forall_not_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_two).
